{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 RCA classification — intended behavior, not a defect\n\n### Proven mechanism\n\nA driven runtime trace of `_completion_precheck` with `LLMBudgetExhaustedError` executed the verifier call, the broad exception arm, remedy selection, and the unconditional force suffix (`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:299-335`). The resulting operator text preserved the resource remedy (`Raise REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS or narrow the task`) and ended with `Override with --force=\"<reason>\".` A control returning a structured `FAIL` executed `close_precheck.py:337-364` and produced findings + evidence-comment coaching with **no force hint**. Thus the ticket is right about RESOURCE/error behavior, but its claim that a genuine FAIL offers force \"today\" is false.\n\n### Rival hypotheses and discriminating results\n\n1. **Classifier/remedy-specific force hint** — rejected. The resource-specific `close_gate_remedy` returns the exception’s own actionable remedy (`src/rebar/llm/failure.py:656-683`), after which the caller appends force independently at `close_precheck.py:330-334`. The runtime line trace observed both operations.\n2. **One shared force hint for FAIL and verifier errors** — rejected for current runtime. The structured-FAIL trace never entered the exception arm and its exact output contained no force text.\n3. **Historical drift removed force only from FAIL while preserving the error bypass** — confirmed statically. Introducing commit `85a77b9cc8` offered force on both any verifier error and FAIL. Commit `9ef37a2bc1` deliberately replaced the FAIL suffix with ticket-comment evidence coaching; its diff removes the FAIL force sentence, while its commit message states no verifier-error/bypass-policy change.\n4. **The RESOURCE hint necessarily causes an agent to force-close without judgment** — not proven. The e369 record shows the hint is actionable and was eventually followed after resource exhaustion, but the actual close comment is explicitly operator-directed and preceded by manual verification of all 14 ACs. Earlier e369 comments explicitly declined force while recovery was underway. This supports salience, not autonomous or unauthorized causation.\n\n### Legitimacy: `intended-behavior`\n\nThe authoritative original epic `slab-drove-stack` requires: `FAIL or missing-LLM blocks (fail-closed) with --force-close bypass`, `--force-close` skips verification/signing, and a closed-without-signature ticket is the durable not-certified signal. Commit `85a77b9cc8` implemented and manually validated the missing/error + force path. The current contract remains explicit in `docs/llm-framework.md:816-824`: FAIL or unavailable LLM / **any verifier error** blocks with a `--force` hint, while force closes without verification/signing. `AGENTS.md:87-90` constrains force as a human-operator judgment escape hatch, not a routine agent move. `tests/unit/test_close_gate_bound_remedy_db1c.py:165-176` likewise names force as a sanctioned operator judgment call for a resource/bound failure.\n\nThe later e369 recovery direction does not supersede this durable contract: it temporarily prohibited unattested closes, then explicitly authorized the resource-exhausted epic’s force-close after manual verification.\n\nTherefore removing or de-emphasizing force specifically for RESOURCE exhaustion would be a **policy/UX change to the documented bypass contract**, not restoration of broken behavior. Recommended disposition: do not repair under this bug. If the operator wants the policy changed, rewrite/reclassify the ticket as a design change and specify which verifier-error classes should still advertise the sanctioned bypass, plus the replacement actionable remedy. The AC requiring a genuine FAIL to keep offering force \"exactly as today\" must also be corrected because current FAIL output does not offer it.\n\nNo caller-dependency sweep or RED contract card was produced: the not-a-bug guard does not unlock Phase 2."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786297693278532001,"uuid":"a7d5fae4-505a-4c09-a128-c0e2c0935f39"}